<div class="space-y-8">
  <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-primary to-secondary text-white rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Custom Domain Setup</h2>
    <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl leading-relaxed opacity-90">
      Point your domain at BizBlasts with two DNS records. Cloudflare issues the certificate.
      Do not create an A record to a home IP address.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-dark mb-6">Records to add</h3>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="min-w-full text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="text-left text-gray-500">
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Name</th>
            <th class="py-2 pr-4 font-medium">Type</th>
            <th class="py-2 font-medium">Target</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">www</code></td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">CNAME</td>
            <td class="py-2"><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded"><%= custom_domain_cname_target %></code></td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4"><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded">@</code></td>
            <td class="py-2 pr-4">ALIAS or flattened CNAME</td>
            <td class="py-2"><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded"><%= custom_domain_cname_target %></code></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-4">
      If the BizBlasts settings page or your setup email lists extra TXT records, add those too.
      Cloudflare uses them only when it needs to confirm you control the domain before issuing the certificate.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-dark mb-3">Registrar has no ALIAS?</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
      <li>Move DNS to Cloudflare (the free plan is enough) and add both records there. Cloudflare flattens a CNAME on @.</li>
      <li>Or keep your registrar, forward the root domain (@) to www, and set only the www CNAME. Visitors who type the bare domain will land on www.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-4">
      Some panels label the root as <code>@</code>, some as a blank name, and some want a trailing dot on the target
      (<code><%= custom_domain_cname_target %>.</code>). Remove any old A or CNAME records for @ and www that point somewhere else.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
